{"seq":24,"slug":"experimental-economics","title":"实验经济学","stage":"DONE","category":"economics-finance","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 实验经济学\n\n很长一段时间里，经济学被认为是一门「不能做实验」的学科。理论用优雅的方程描述人如何在约束下最优化，而检验这些方程只能依赖历史数据——可现实中无数因素同时变动，谁也无法把「价格上涨」这一个原因从混杂的世界里干净地剥离出来。实验经济学的全部价值，就在于把实验室的受控逻辑搬进经济问题：在一个被精心设计的环境里，让真实的人面对真实的货币激励做选择，从而把理论的预测和人的实际行为直接对峙。\n\n本 hub 沿着四条逐步递进的主线展开。第一条是「方法论」：它回答最根本的问题——一个经济实验凭什么算数。诱导价值理论、控制与随机化、实验室与田野和自然实验之间的取舍，构成了后面一切结论的地基；没有干净的设计，再漂亮的数据也只是噪声。\n\n第二条主线转向「个体决策」：当人独自面对风险、面对今天与未来的取舍时，他真的像期望效用理论假设的那样理性吗？大量实验给出的答案是否定的——确定性效应、损失厌恶、双曲贴现、偏好反转，这些被反复验证的异象，逼着理论从「人是理性的」退到「人是可预测地非理性的」。\n\n第三条主线进入「博弈与市场」：人不是孤岛，决策嵌在与他人的互动里。最后通牒、独裁者、信任、公共品这些博弈揭示了纯自利模型解释不了的慷慨与惩罚；而市场与拍卖实验则展示了另一面——在合适的制度下，一群并不完美理性的人竟能让市场迅速收敛到理论均衡。\n\n第四条主线伸向「应用与前沿」：实验的洞见如何离开实验室。行为政策与助推把这些发现变成真实世界里的默认选项设计；神经经济学钻到决策的生理底层去寻找机制；而在线实验与可重复性危机，则迫使整个学科重新审视自己的证据标准。\n\n四条主线并非平行，而是层层递进：方法论是地基，个体决策是单人砖块，博弈与市场把砖块砌成互动结构，应用与前沿则检验整座建筑能否经受真实世界与科学规范的双重考验。读完整个 hub，你会理解的不只是一串有趣的实验结果，而是一种用受控证据逼问经济理论的思维方式。建议从[方法论](1_methodology/_INTRODUCTION.md)读起，它会为后面所有章节提供共同的语言。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"methodology","title":"方法论","docCount":3,"url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/methodology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-methods","title":"实验经济学导论与方法","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/methodology/intro-and-methods"},{"seq":2,"slug":"experimental-design-control","title":"实验设计与控制","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/methodology/experimental-design-control"},{"seq":3,"slug":"lab-field-natural-experiments","title":"实验室、田野与自然实验","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/methodology/lab-field-natural-experiments"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"individual-decision","title":"个体决策","docCount":3,"url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/individual-decision","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"risk-uncertainty-decisions","title":"风险与不确定性下的决策","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/individual-decision/risk-uncertainty-decisions"},{"seq":2,"slug":"time-preference-intertemporal","title":"时间偏好与跨期选择","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/individual-decision/time-preference-intertemporal"},{"seq":3,"slug":"preference-elicitation-anomalies","title":"偏好引出与决策异象","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/individual-decision/preference-elicitation-anomalies"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"games-markets","title":"博弈与市场","docCount":3,"url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/games-markets","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"social-preferences-ultimatum-trust","title":"社会偏好（最后通牒·独裁者·信任博弈）","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/games-markets/social-preferences-ultimatum-trust"},{"seq":2,"slug":"public-goods-cooperation","title":"公共品与合作","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/games-markets/public-goods-cooperation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"market-auction-experiments","title":"市场与拍卖实验","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/games-markets/market-auction-experiments"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"applications-frontiers","title":"应用与前沿","docCount":3,"url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/applications-frontiers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"behavioral-policy-nudge","title":"行为政策与助推","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/applications-frontiers/behavioral-policy-nudge"},{"seq":2,"slug":"neuroeconomics","title":"神经经济学","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/applications-frontiers/neuroeconomics"},{"seq":3,"slug":"online-experiments-replicability","title":"在线实验与可重复性","url":"/h/economics-finance/experimental-economics/applications-frontiers/online-experiments-replicability"}]}]}